","covered in forests of giant ferns","with a wizard's tower on its highest peak","where every child is taught to speak with seals","the last harbour of the cloud-sailors","whose cliffs glow faintly after dark","where merfolk trade pearls for iron nails","that drifts a few miles east every century","home to the finest shipwrights in the known world","where a fallen star still smoulders in the hills","with the ruins of a library swallowed by the waves","where the fairy market opens one night a year","ruled by a queen who has not aged in three hundred years","known for its glass-blowers and their enchanted lanterns","where dragons once came to lay their eggs in the warm sand"],"tropical":["a ring of white sand around a turquoise lagoon","where sea turtles come ashore to nest each spring","fringed by mangroves full of tiny bright crabs","where the reef is close enough to snorkel from the beach","known for its sweet mangoes and slow afternoons","with a waterfall tumbling into a jungle pool","where flamingos wade in the salt flats at sunset","famous for its pink sand beaches","a sleepy fishing village with brightly painted boats","where the only traffic is a bicycle and a goat","ringed by coral gardens and lazy sea turtles","home to a family of friendly dolphins","where the market sells coconuts, limes and grilled fish","with a volcano that has slept for a thousand years","where hummingbirds feed on the hibiscus by every door","just big enough for a lighthouse and a lemon grove","where the water is clear enough to count the starfish","with a hidden cove only the locals know about","where fishermen still sail out in wooden canoes","known for its rainy mornings and golden evenings","with a sandbar that appears only at low tide","where parrots squabble in the banyan trees","where the ferry comes twice a week, if the weather allows","fringed with coconut palms and warm shallow water","with a night market lit by paper lanterns","where whales pass close by in the winter months","famous for its vanilla farms and spice gardens","with a blue hole so deep no diver has reached the bottom"],"mysterious":["that appears on the charts only at midsummer","where the lighthouse still burns, though no keeper has lived there for a century","wrapped in a fog that never fully lifts","where every compass spins and the clocks run slow","found empty, with supper still warm on the tables","where a bell tolls at midnight with no one to pull the rope","whose standing stones move a little each night","where the birds fall silent all at once","that sailors refuse to name aloud","marked on old maps with a single word: Beware","where footprints in the sand lead into the sea and never back","with a stone circle no one remembers building","where the tide goes out and does not return for a day","home to a hermit who knows everyone's name","where lanterns are seen moving on the moors at night","whose only village was abandoned overnight","that no two maps place in the same spot","where the well water tastes faintly of iron","with a door carved into the cliff that will not open","where a choir can be heard singing under the waves","circled by ravens from dawn to dusk","where the ferryman asks for no coin, only a secret","with a library of books written in no known language","where every clock stopped at the same minute fifty years ago","known only from a page torn out of a captain's log","whose shadow on the water points the wrong way","where someone keeps the gardens tidy, though nobody lives there","that the seabirds will not land on","with a shipwreck that turns up on a different beach every year","reached by stepping stones that are never in the same place twice"],"pirate":["where smugglers once hid their barrels in the sea caves","with a cove too narrow for the navy's ships","where a captain's gold is said to lie under the third palm","once the hideout of a fearsome pirate queen","where the old fort's cannons still face the harbour","known for its sea shanties and noisy parrots","where every map ends with a big red X","ringed by reefs that have sunk a dozen ships","with a hollow tree used as a pirates' post office","where castaways carve their names into the rocks","home to a crew of retired buccaneers and their cats","where the treasure has been buried and dug up four times","guarded by a grumpy old parrot who knows the way to the gold","with a cave that only opens at the lowest tide","where a ghost ship drops anchor every full moon","famous for its black-sailed sloops","where no honest sailor ties up after dark","home to a market selling stolen silks and spices","with a skull-shaped rock at the harbour mouth","where the navy's last three captains were marooned","with a lookout post that spots ships a day before they arrive","where mutineers built a town out of their own wrecked ship","where an old sea captain sells maps to anywhere but here","once a navy jail, until the inmates took it over","with a lagoon full of sunken ships and curious fish","known for parrots that sing sea shanties","where a pirate king once held court in a cave","with tunnels running from the beach to the old governor's house","where the tide hides a staircase cut into the cliff"],"cosy":["with one tea shop, two ferries a day and far too many ducks","where the post arrives by rowing boat and everybody waves","known for its summer fair and prize-winning pumpkins","with a bakery that sells out of buns by ten","where the bunnies outnumber the people","with a lighthouse that doubles as a library","where the evening ferry plays music for the whole harbour","with apple trees on every corner and a pond full of frogs","home to the friendliest shopkeeper in the archipelago","where the café stays open until the last fishing boat comes in","famous for its flower festival every spring","where the beach is perfect for picnics","with a tiny campsite and room for one more tent","where fireflies light up the meadows on summer nights","known for its jam contest and fiercely competitive grannies","with a hot spring, a hammock and nowhere to be","where the shop sells everything from fishing rods to birthday cakes","with a stargazing hill and a bench for every friend","where the only rule is to be kind to the frogs","home to a lazy cat who considers herself the mayor","with a little orchard and a pier for watching sunsets","where winter brings a harbour-wide snowball fight","where the rock pools are full of tiny crabs","with a garden for every cottage","where the cherry blossom turns the whole hill pink","known for its cosy autumn evenings and pumpkin soup","where neighbours trade vegetables over the garden fence","with fishing in the morning and cocoa at night"]}}}